      "reasons": [
        "The definition states that “Burned out describes a state of poor work-related and psychological wellbeing,” but the packet does not explicitly define “burned out” as a “state of poor” wellbeing; it only reports associated outcomes (e.g., distress, depression/anxiety, lower subjective wellbeing) and related attitudes (e.g., less job commitment, considering leaving) in teachers.",
        "The packet’s support is specific to “burned-out teachers” rather than a general description of “burned out” across all contexts, so the definition’s broad wording (“work-related and psychological wellbeing”) is not tightly supported as written."
